The function was already minimal, so this rewrite changes little. It indexes through `fields.data()` instead of `operator[]`, and keeps the same bounds check and the same `FIT_NULL` return. The speed difference will be negligible at best.

```cpp
FieldDefinition* MesgDefinition::GetFieldByIndex(const FIT_UINT16 index)
{
    const size_t count = fields.size();
    if (static_cast<size_t>(index) < count)
        return fields.data() + index;

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```